%S A402078 12,12,12,18,24,30,40,54,60,78,88,102,120,138,156,176,198,220,246,272,
%T A402078 300,330,360,390,426,460,492,532,570,606,650,690,736,780,828,876,924,
%U A402078 972,1026,1074,1134,1182,1240,1300,1356,1420,1480,1542,1608,1674,1740
%N A402078 a(n) is the smallest abundant number (A005101) that is equal to the sum of n distinct deficient numbers (A005100).
%C A402078 Offset is 2 because for n = 1, a number cannot be both abundant and deficient.
%C A402078 Similar to A401272 but for abundant numbers, to A401273 but for deficient numbers, and to A401274 but for deficient sums of abundant numbers.
%e A402078 1, 2, 4, 5, 9, 11 are deficient numbers, 12 is an abundant number, and a(2) = a(3) = a(4) = 1 + 11 = 1 + 2 + 9 = 1 + 2 + 4 + 5 = 12.
%Y A402078 Cf. A005100, A005101.
%Y A402078 Cf. A401272, A401273, A401274.
%K A402078 nonn,new
%O A402078 2,1
%A A402078 _Bernard Schott_, Nov 12 2026
%E A402078 More terms from _Sean A. Irvine_, Nov 23 2026
